1. The angle progression is algebraic, not log/exp. In the fixed-n family the angle is exactly atan(2nm/(m²−n²)), which falls like 2n/m. For n=2 that is about 229/m degrees: the last point sits at θ·m = 229.1, converging on 4 rad = 229.2°. Power fit θ ∝ m^-0.988, R² = 0.9999. So it's the parabola family, not a logarithm.
2. Along the chain, curvature follows a clean power law: |κ| ∝ s^-1.238, R² = 0.993. A spiral — but none of the familiar ones: clothoid is s⁺¹, log spiral s⁻¹, circle s⁰. That's the "larger group" you suspected; it just isn't the exponential one.
